<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH JULY CPI RISES REVISED 2.3 PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>DUTCH JULY CPI RISES REVISED 2.3 PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch consumer price index (CPI) rose a revised 0.5 percent in July from June, giving a 2.3 percent year-on-year rise, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.</p>
<p>The CBS decided to publish a revised set of July CPI data because data originally published on Friday had been based on an incorrect calculation of the annual rise in housing rents.</p>
<p>The original data had shown a 0.6 percent month-on-month</p>
<p>increase in the July CPI and a year-on-year rise of 2.4 pct.</p>
<p>DUTCH CONSUMER PRICE INFLATION    July 97	 June 97  July 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI pct change	     0.5 (0.6)     -0.4	0.4</p>
<p> Year-on-year CPI pct change	2.3 (2.4)	2.2	2.2</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		  119.3 (119.4)  118.7    116.6</p>
<p>EU-HARMONISED DUTCH INFLATION</p>
<p> Monthly CPI pct change	     0.2 (0.3)     -0.5     -0.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year CPI pct change	2.1 (2.2)	1.7	1.5</p>
<p> Index (base 1996)		  101.6 (101.7)  101.4     99.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Previously published July figures are given in</p>
<p>brackets.</p>
<p>The detailed non-harmonised index figures were:</p>
<p>					 Weighting  July 97	  June 97</p>
<p> Food, drink, tobacco		    180    111.7	    111.5</p>
<p> Clothes, shoes			     72     85.5	     94.5</p>
<p> Rent, heating, lighting		 261    136.9 (137.3)  132.7</p>
<p> Furniture, household appliances etc. 80    107.0	    107.0</p>
<p> Medical care				  6    120.7	    120.6</p>
<p> Transport, communication		144    121.3	    119.7</p>
<p> Leisure, education			107    107.7	    107.8</p>
<p> Other goods, services		   113    119.8	    118.5</p>
<p> Consumer taxes, govt. services	 37    148.2	    154.4</p>
